 "changes": [
  "Textures: replaced in place (same names and GUIDs): T_Base_Barbed_A_px.png, T_Base_ChainLink_A_px.png, T_Base_Rust_A_px.png, T_Kpp_Barbed_A_px.png, T_Kpp_ChainLink_A_px.png, T_Road_Barbed_A_px.png, T_Road_ChainLink_A_px.png, T_Yard_Barbed_A_px.png, T_Yard_ChainLink_A_px.png - the netting with 2 px wires in 12.5 cm diamonds (was 1 px in 6.25 cm), the barbed and rusty wire 2 px; the same sizes and strand positions, the models' UVs unchanged",
  "Forest_Materials.json: 7 new materials at the end: M_Fence_Concrete, M_Fence_Props, M_Fence_Panel, M_Fence_ChainLink, M_Fence_Barbed, M_Fence_ChainBarbed, M_Fence_Razor (the cut-outs one-sided: doubleSided false)",
  "Forest_Materials.json: doubleSided true -> false (in place): M_Base_ChainLink, M_Base_Barbed, M_Base_Rust, M_Kpp_ChainLink, M_Kpp_Barbed, M_Yard_ChainLink, M_Yard_Barbed, M_Road_ChainLink, M_Road_Barbed - their models carry the netting and the wire as two faces back to back (the base and far ones in one plane, the kpp, yard and road ones 1.2 mm apart); drawn two-sided, both faces showed from either side and fought for the depth (the shimmer); one-sided, each face shows from its own side",
  "Forest_Layout.json rocks: - 213 FenceChain (Update 3's chain-link fence of the base: the PO-2 concrete fence stands on its lines now)",
